<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Lenco boosts interim shr, no div.</title>
<headline>Lenco boosts interim shr, no div.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended Sept 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     25.14	 vs 9.00</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   21.99	 vs 7.26 loss</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit	  26.26	 vs 1.46 loss</p>
<p>    Tax			  4.47	 vs 5.89</p>
<p>    Interest paid	    3.07	 vs 8.55</p>
<p>    Turnover		 333.26	 vs 382.77</p>
<p>Full name: Lenco Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	2.10	 vs 14.37 loss</p>
<p>NOTE -  The exceptional item reflects the sale of Amshoe, which incurred heavy losses last year.</p>
<p>The group, which does not declare interim dividends, said that the second half of its financial year was traditionally stronger and early indications of sales and forward order books were encouraging.</p>
<p>It expected higher profits for the full year.</p>
<p>Earnings are before exceptional items.</p>
<p>-- Cape Town newsroom +27 21 25-2238</p>
</text>
